Subject: InsetsPolicy: give a dialog no caption bar inset, and a freeform window its status bar

The DSA agent gives each freeform task a caption bar and a status bar inset source, both as high
as the host window's title bar. InsetsSource.calculateArbitraryInsets gives a caption bar
source's full height to every window of the task, wherever the window is, so a dialog (Dialog,
AlertDialog, the date and time pickers, a context menu) got the band's height as its top inset
although it sits below the band. DecorView then moved the dialog's content down by that much
inside its surface, while touch stayed where the window is: the dialog was drawn 58 px below the
place that takes its taps.

enforceInsetsPolicyForTarget now removes the caption bar source from a window that is not as
large as its parent, or that the window manager lays out below the band (it fits the caption bar
or the status bar). The task's full-size edge-to-edge window keeps it. Android 16 had the same
rule behind its relativeInsets flag, which its published builds turn on; Android 17 dropped it.

A window in a floating windowing mode keeps the system bar sources (status bars, navigation bars
and the caption bar) and the IME, not only the caption bar and the IME, so an app that pads its
toolbar by its status bar inset keeps it below the title bar. make-image.py made this second
change as a dex edit of the published services.jar until the image took the framework build's.

Applies to frameworks/base at 94b4c163b7dfe5ce3607f7bb8456f9573f7de57d (Android 17).
---
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/InsetsPolicy.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/InsetsPolicy.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/InsetsPolicy.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/InsetsPolicy.java
@@ -417,6 +417,28 @@ class InsetsPolicy {
             }
         }

+        // DSA: a caption bar source reaches only the windows that cover the task's caption band.
+        // InsetsSource.calculateArbitraryInsets gives a caption bar source's full height to every
+        // window, wherever the window is (b/254128050), so a dialog in a freeform task got the
+        // band's height as its top inset although it sits below the band, and DecorView moved
+        // its content down by that much inside its surface while touch stayed where the window
+        // is. A window that is not as large as its parent (a dialog, a context menu) or that the
+        // window manager lays out below the band (it fits the caption bar or the status bar,
+        // whose source the agent gives the same frame) does not get the source; the task's
+        // full-size edge-to-edge window keeps it. Android 16 still had this rule behind its
+        // relativeInsets flag, which its published builds turn on, and Android 17 dropped it.
+        if (!attrs.isFullscreen() || (attrs.getFitInsetsTypes()
+                & (Type.captionBar() | Type.statusBars())) != 0) {
+            for (int i = state.sourceSize() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
+                if (state.sourceAt(i).getType() == Type.captionBar()) {
+                    if (state == originalState) {
+                        state = new InsetsState(originalState);
+                    }
+                    state.removeSourceAt(i);
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
         final SparseArray<InsetsSourceProvider> providers = mStateController.getSourceProviders();
         final int windowType = attrs.type;
         for (int i = providers.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
@@ -435,7 +457,13 @@ class InsetsPolicy {
